        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Apsley Cherry-Garrard\n- Works: The Worst Journey in the World\n- Events: Antarctic expedition\n- Topics: exploration literature, human suffering under extreme conditions\n\nFacts:\n- Apsley George Benet Cherry-Garrard was born on 2 January 1886 and died on 18 May 1959.\n- Apsley Cherry-Garrard was an English explorer of Antarctica.\n- Apsley Cherry-Garrard, a member of the expedition, wrote and published The Worst Journey in the World in 1922.\n- The Worst Journey in the World earned wide praise for its frank treatment of the expedition's difficulties, the causes of its disastrous outcome, and the meaning of human suffering under extreme conditions.",
